{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you're here because of pain at your G-tube site. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the pain has been getting worse. I ran out of my oxycodone a few days ago, and Tylenol just isn’t helping at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had this tube for a while due to your gastric bypass and hypoglycemia, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and I’ve had this pain before. I’ve been admitted a few times already. The last CT showed inflammation, but no infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right, and your tube was exchanged, but that didn’t help much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it didn’t. I tried naproxen for a bit because it helped, but then I was told NSAIDs could cause ulcers, so I stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s correct. Given your history of ulcers, we avoid NSAIDs. We’ll start you on oxycodone again to manage the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just need something that works. The pain is constant and sharp."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you 10 mg every four hours as needed. We’ll also monitor for any signs of infection or complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there any sign of infection now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, your site looks clean—no redness or swelling. Your labs are stable too. No fever, and your white count is normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been keeping up with my tube feeds, but they do irritate the site a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on NutriHep at 50 cc/hr for now. Staying nourished is important, especially with your hypoglycemia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been checking my blood sugar at home. It’s been okay as long as I keep feeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll continue monitoring your intake and output. You’re passing gas and having bowel movements?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been going regularly. No nausea or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. We’ll encourage you to walk around a bit to keep your lungs and circulation healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been up a little. I feel okay, just the pain is really distracting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2173-09-18 01:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll reassess your pain in an hour. Let the nurse know if it’s not improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2173-09-18 02:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the pain now after the first dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2173-09-18 02:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still there, but not as intense. I can actually relax a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2173-09-18 02:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We’ll keep you on this schedule. No need for IV pain meds since the oral dose is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2173-09-18 02:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I’d rather avoid IV if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2173-09-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Vital signs are stable—no fever, heart rate and blood pressure are fine. Pain still manageable?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2173-09-18 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, as long as I take the oxycodone on time. I’ve had a few doses overnight and slept okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2173-09-18 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep monitoring. You have a few specialist appointments coming up, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2173-09-18 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I have a second opinion with a bariatric surgeon, then with Dr. Chen, and then at the Pancreas and Liver Institute to talk about pancreatectomy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2173-09-18 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right. Those might help figure out a long-term solution. This pain seems to be chronic inflammation without infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2173-09-18 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just want it to stop. I can’t keep coming back every time I run out of pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2173-09-18 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’re not just treating the symptom—we’re working toward a plan. For now, we’ll keep you comfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you today. You’ve been stable, pain is controlled with oral meds, and no complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I get a refill on the oxycodone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re prescribing 60 tablets, one every four hours as needed. But please don’t exceed that without talking to your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. What about my tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Resume NutriHep at 45 cc/hour. Monitor your blood sugar closely, especially if you’re not eating by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your regular medications—fluoxetine, lansoprazole, sucralfate, rifaximin—continue as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the pain gets worse again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your surgeon or return to the ER if pain doesn’t improve within a few hours, or if you develop fever, vomiting, or signs of dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch for that. And I have my follow-up appointments scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Rest, stay hydrated, and keep moving around at home. Avoid driving while on pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll have someone help me at home. Thank you for getting the pain under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2173-09-19 00:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll make sure your records are sent to your specialists. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2173-09-19 12:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before you leave. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2173-09-19 12:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, pain is mild now. I’ve been walking and drinking fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2173-09-19 12:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Discharge papers are ready. Follow up with your surgeon as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2173-09-19 12:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2173-09-19 12:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy. We’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2173-09-18 01:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2173-09-19 12:51:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for severe pain at her G-tube site, which had worsened after running out of oxycodone. She reported prior episodes with similar presentations, and previous imaging showed non-specific inflammation without infection. During this admission, she was restarted on oral oxycodone with good pain control and continued her home tube feeds (NutriHep) without complications. She remained afebrile and hemodynamically stable, with no signs of infection or bleeding. IV Dilaudid was available but not required. She was discharged home with a prescription for oxycodone, instructions to resume feeds at 45 cc/hour, monitor blood glucose, and follow up with her bariatric surgeon and other specialists for ongoing evaluation of chronic pain. Discharge planning included clear instructions on when to seek medical help and avoidance of driving while on pain medication.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain, other specified site",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Other and unspecified postsurgical nonabsorption",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Other chronic nonalcoholic liver disease",
      "Personal history of peptic ulcer disease",
      "Personal history of Methicillin resistant Staphylococcus aureus"
    ]
  }
}
